            <ArticleTitle>Urogynecologic causes of chronic pelvic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>685-98</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many women with CPP undergo lengthy evaluations and sometimes empiric operative procedures only to continue to have pain for which no clear source can be found. Occasionally, a review of urinary symptoms may be the key to initiating a diagnostic and therapeutic course that reveals a urologic cause for their pain. Appropriate treatment directed to the urinary disorder may lead to improvement and potentially obviate gynecologic surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
